ressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA MASAOU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUHARA MUNEKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SATO MAKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU KENJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI HIDEO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA FUMIKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>DOKE, TAKASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>GYOBU, SHOICHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MATSUDA, MASAOU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUHARA, MUNEKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, MAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHIMIZU, KENJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>TAKEUCHI, HIDEO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, FUMIKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flame-retardant polyester fiber which satisfies the above expressions (1) to (3) and comprises a phosphorus compound copolyester having a phosphorus content of 500 to 50,000 ppm; a woven or knitted flame-retardant polyester fabric comprising the flame-retardant polyester fiber as at least part thereof; and a woven or knitted suede fabric obtained by raising the woven or knitted flame-retardant polyester fabric. Due to these constitutions, the flame-retardant polyester fiber, the woven or knitted fabric, and the woven or knitted suede fabric are excellent in dyeability, thermal stability, and mechanical properties including wearing resistance.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une fibre de polyester anti-feu qui remplit les conditions (1) à (3), comprenant un copolyester à base de phosphore. La teneur en phosphore est comprise entre 500 et 50 000 ppm. L'invention concerne en outre un tissu de polyester anti-feu tissé ou maillé composé au moins partiellement du type de fibre considéré, et un tissu suède tissé ou maillé obtenu par relevage du tissu en polyester anti-feu tissé ou maillé. Les conditions ci-dessus font que la fibre de polyester anti-feu, le tissu tissé ou maillé et le tissu suède tissé ou maillé possèdent d'excellentes caractéristiques du point de vue de l'aptitude à la teinture, de la stabilité thermique et des propriétés mécaniques, y compris la résistance à l'usure.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>